#X obj 2100 1700 r \$0-page;
#X obj 2100 1750 outlet;
#X obj 2400 380 declare -lib pdlua;
#X text 20 1820 Steps are cut from c_clock's beat phase times four \, never from its beat bang \, which tops out at 14.3 a second (ref/module/tempo.md). The threshold is a twelfth of a step \, where u_tempo's MIDI pulse for that sixteenth falls \, so a step and the clock the 404 follows land in one block. Debounces 0 \, as in c_clock., f 58;
#X text 20 2010 Every track reads this one counter. Per-track subdivision would give each track its own multiplier on the same phase in place of the times four \, and its own counter., f 58;
#X text 300 670 PLAY starts at step 1: the counter parks at -1 so the next is 0 \, whatever the last step. The spigot shuts for one logical instant \, so a step cut before c_clock's phase reset cannot fire as step 1. STOP and panic stop it and put the playhead out., f 44;
#X text 520 1100 On each step the Lua answers fire with every track not at 0 \, in one logical instant: m_404's budget passes sixteen at once and drops beyond that \, never queues (ref/device/sp404.md). Then the playhead moves., f 44;
#X text 1000 1450 The rules live in c_steps.lua: the pattern \, the step rule \, the velocity levels \, the selected track and level \, and which tracks fire on a step. c_steps-lua is its Pd face. This file keeps the clock \, the transport \, and the cords to m_404 \, g_grid and u_state. Edit the rules there \, not here: test/gate/lua/c_steps_test.lua runs them without Pd. A press the Lua does not know is fail c_steps bad-selector \, and a Lua error fail c_steps lua-<selector> (C-12)., f 50;
#X text 1600 1500 The pattern is one auto key \, section-1-<part>: 256 velocities \, track by track (ref/module/state.md). The Lua takes a restore and answers with the pattern \, which is put straight back: a load never fills u_state's live store \, so a key nobody re-puts is dropped at the next flush \, and a short or malformed line is repaired by the same put., f 40;
#X text 2100 1450 At load the Lua answers init with the page's selection and a bang on its last outlet \, which shuts the spigot. No bang means it never loaded -- pdlua missing \, or an error in the Lua -- and fail c_steps no-lua says so on the screen \, the only place a device with no console can., f 40;
